# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for a -DFW_SANITIZE=thread build of the tests:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=cmake/tsan.supp build/bin/FrameworkTests
#
# Third-party code only, one reason per entry. Nothing here may name Framework or MafiaNet code:
# a report there is a finding.
#
# Format: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions

# Tracy starts its worker threads from one static initializer and constructs its allocator's span
# cache from a later one in the same file, so the constructor writes zeros under a thread already
# allocating. Before main(), inside vendors/tracy.
race:tracy::global_cache_t::global_cache_t
